WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:07.140
The United Nations Film Board presents The
Eternal Fight

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.340
[Narrator:] Deliver us.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.460
Deliver us from the plague, from hunger, from
war.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.360
This has been the cry of mankind throughout
all time.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.670
Blinded by ignorance, filled with terror,
he lashed out against the black plague with

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.900
witchcraft, against typhus with superstition.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.660
And so maddened efforts to stem the terrifying
ravages of epidemics, prejudice, and intolerance,

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:04.600
too often resulted in cruel and vicious treatment
of those suffering from contagious diseases.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.320
Despite the raging panic of ignorance, the
lurking danger of contagion,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.420
scientists of many nations went to work.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.320
Painfully they labored to nurse the flickering
light of research into a broad searchlight

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.480
of knowledge,

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:33.860
using every means of communication to share
their findings with each other.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:42.420
It was the Dutchman, Leeuwenhoek, whose research
helped provide scientists everywhere

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.930
with a new and powerful vision of the microscope.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.220
Now at last the hidden enemy could be examined
under the probing searchlight of science.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.180
The hunt was on for contagious diseases and
their causes, wherever they existed.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
[Narrator:] Spallanzani in Italy pioneered
the work on the origin and growth of microscopic organisms.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.420
He proved that fermentation did not take place in sealed containers,

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:23.900
but occurred only through contact with the
microorganisms present in the air.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.440
Jenner, in England, painstakingly evolved
the basic principles of vaccination,

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:47.800
and a little British girl was the first to
wince at the sting of a vaccinating needle.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.520
And Pasteur in France, his was the brilliant
research that resulted in the discovery

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.120
of the causes of contagious diseases.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:11.700
He proved that microbes were at the root of such diseases, and thus medical science marched forward

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:17.340
bringing light where once there had been darkness,
hope where once there had been despair.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:24.900
And in Germany, Koch identified and isolated the Koch bacillus and the dreaded germ of cholera.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.040
Across the sea in America, Walter Reed and
his colleagues sought to prove that the mosquito

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.020
was the sole transmitter of yellow fever.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.600
They offered their lives, and won.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.560
And so the old prejudices were smashed and the free exchange of information forged modern weapons,

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.320
like the ancient diseases of mankind.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.260
Then, in the course of the nineteenth century,
the world underwent a striking change.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.820
It gave birth to the Industrial Revolution...
transformed man's way of life.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.580
Men, women, and children crowded into cities,
became part of a vast machine.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:09.920
Deprived of sun and fresh nourishment of the
country, men's bodies rusted,

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.600
became more vulnerable to contagion.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:23.640
New means of transportation brought the world
tight and close together, tremendous

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.480
making it one and congested city.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.160
From a disease-infected zone the traveler
now became, unwittingly, a carrier of deadly germs.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.580
Wherever he went the germs stayed and spread.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:01.800
Epidemics break out far from the known infected
areas.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:06.820
Country to country, continent to continent,
the deadly cargo of microbes is transported,

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:11.080
menacing on a vast scale the very existence
of humanity.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:21.220
Mass infection and epidemics are a threat
to every city, to every nation.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:25.400
Scientific and medical work on a local scale
are no longer enough.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:35.160
Thus, in common defense, nations joined an international agreement in the battle against epidemics.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:40.720
Medical agreements and protective measures
are formulated, quarantine measures extended,

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.920
frontier controls set up.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:47.920
When an epidemic strikes, that country is
subjected to special restrictive measures.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:55.380
Suspected carriers are isolated, and step-by-step, the dangers of contagion grow less and less.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.120
War!

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:23.860
The first great World War, like all wars,
sucking mankind down to misery and death.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.260
And together with war, pestilence, and disease,

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.680
epidemics wreak havoc greater than war, wipe out civilian populations.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:35.600
The problem is everywhere and must be dealt
with internationally.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:47.640
A network of medical information is swiftly
organized through radio, newspapers, pamphlets, bulletins.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:53.800
The League of Nations spreads information
that all may fight the contagion of diseases.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:15.420
In Geneva, this immense storehouse of information becomes part of the arsenal of embattled doctors

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.040
and scientists everywhere.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:24.180
Heath reports are received, checked, filed,
collated, and sent out again ready for use.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:28.860
Because now trains are entering and leaving
stations.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.640
Ships leave and dock at foreign ports.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:39.120
Millions live, work, and suffer.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.540
For this sailor it's always hard to say goodbye.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:51.040
Harder still when your wife is sick, burning
with fever, and you have to pull anchor.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.780
There's nothing to worry about, you say.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.140
She'll be all right in a couple of days.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:59.400
Besides, you need the job.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:17.440
But neither of you suspect...typhus.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.440
The black plague.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.800
And so goodbye.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.060
Both have become carriers of death-dealing
germs.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:48.220
Germs that will blast the lives of shipmates.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:55.120
Germs traveling across seas to start a terrible
epidemic at any moment, any place.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:18.760
Epidemic starts anytime, anyplace, wherever
you are, wherever she is now in a hospital.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:22.040
There are no doubts, it is contagious.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.100
Immediate action, a life at stake, and though
she might infect or has already infected,

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.200
Who is she?

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:40.020
A friend.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:40.660
Her kinfolk.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:45.740
Send the alert everywhere, to every nation,
to every port, in every language.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.620
Easy enough to locate all ships which left
the area before the outbreak.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:51.260
Message to all ships at sea.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:55.399
The quarantine service must know the health condition of your ships in every port.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:10:03.800
Every day, almost every moment, for epidemic
strikes any time, any place, wherever you are.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.820
A protective mechanism is set in motion.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:44.160
The quarantine service issues the necessary orders to the ship for investigation and control.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.020
The ship is stopped, the sick man brought
ashore.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.640
All others are fully protected by inoculation.

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:41.740
And now the ship is thoroughly disinfected.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.980
Rats are hunted out of their hiding places.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.240
Cyanide gas does the trick.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:51.900
Teams of specialists fumigate the boat from
stem to stern, from staterooms to the hold.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:57.020
Everything completely disinfected before the
ship is able to sail on in safety.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:29.660
Such cooperation protects mankind from recurring
epidemics.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:34.620
International cooperation provides immediate
action to smash a swift-striking enemy.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.440
Today there are no distances.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:49.600
Today the aeroplane links continents as trains
link cities.

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:55.340
Today the peoples of the world are one people
joined by wings over the globe.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:20.720
Today people of all races, of every level,
move from country to country in a matter of hours.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:34.040
Today vital medical control is established
around the modern points of international exchange, the airports.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:40.060
The network of health information and services
has been extended here from the seaport organization.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:41.579
But is this sufficient?

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:46.080
How long does it take before a potential epidemic
can be detected?

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:03.160
From one continent to another, only a few
hours flying time.

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:08.760
But cholera takes longer to show itself.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.200
And yellow fever three to six days.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.900
And the incubation period of smallpox from
seven to 16 days.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:32.880
Passengers in a modern plane look perfectly
healthy.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:36.120
They are, but how do we know?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:41.880
That little girl, when she got the doll, did
she receive germs as well?

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:47.380
Some passengers may be germ carriers, perhaps
already in the incubation stage.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.800
They'll reach their destination before any
symptoms show.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:55.339
The quarantine service can't keep every plane
and passenger grounded for several days

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.370
to effect thorough medical control.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.760
Today, that system of defense is no longer
enough.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:04.680
Today, epidemics must be crushed at the very
source.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:24.140
Unfortunately, in some countries, contagious
diseases exist in an endemic state.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.140
That is, permanently.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:32.460
India, for instance, has certain areas that
are always infected with cholera.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.340
This plague can extend to Western Europe.

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:43.740
In Africa, some forms of malaria still rage,
germs that might easily be transmitted to South America.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:51.720
And cholera in Japan could strike suddenly
at the west coast of the United States.

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:03.700
Permanently infected zones are localized but
may cover large areas of territory,

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:05.240
sometimes entire continents.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:10.240
Modern transport poses new dangers of complete
universal contagion.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:17.240
The struggle against epidemics is a global
one,

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:19.860
for the danger of death is worldwide.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.220
Then...what is the answer?

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:41.620
Within the framework of the United Nations, a new organization exists

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.280
to promote the welfare of all people:

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:45.400
the World Health Organization.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:53.500
It its first assembly, July 1948, Director-General Dr. Chisholm declared that this organization was physically prepared

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:58.360
to raise the health level of all people and
to forever destroy the human afflictions of

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.160
of malaria, cholera, tuberculosis, and syphilis.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:07.940
The prime objective of the World Health Organization
is the fight against disease on a global scale.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:20.200
The representatives of nearly every nation
have signed the great Charter of Health.

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:23.980
This means an organization with the authority
and means to act.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:28.420
Epidemics, no matter what part of the world they may infect, are a potential danger

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:29.700
to all other nations.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:36.400
The World Health Organization will make full use of every existing means: education, prevention, cure.

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:41.940
All peoples of every race and belief will
be helped by doctors from all races and nations.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:45.840
A tremendous movement of world solidarity
is now born.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:49.640
Inoculation already widely used will be extended.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.960
Millions of people will be given prophylactic
injections.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:57.340
A worldwide system of medical control will
exist everywhere.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:21.880
Enormous quantities of serums, vaccines, new and powerful drugs such as penicillin and sulfonamides

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:25.440
are already being manufactured at increasingly lower costs.

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:29.760
Crates of ampules are shipped to all parts
of the world, ready for emergency measures.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:34.340
A constant flow of up-to-date information
from every nation in every tongue

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:38.540
now makes it possible to apply the latest discoveries of modern medicine.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:52.140
Cholera broke out in Egypt shortly before
the first assembly meeting of the World Health Organization.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:58.900
The first cases were instantly reported, and
from Cairo every nation was immediately alerted.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:30.080
New York was then the clearinghouse for the
incoming orders for vaccines and equipment

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.780
needed to fight the epidemic that was menacing
Egypt.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.020
Dr. Calderon issued orders.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:40.280
How about sulfadiazine, serums, needles, syringes,
anything else?

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:41.520
Anything.

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:42.860
Don't worry about the payment.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:45.400
The World Health Organization will pay.

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:47.440
Let's get going fast.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.340
The answer was swift.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:52.840
From France, China, Indochina, Soviet Union,
and the United States,

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:55.360
vaccines were shipped by the fastest means.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:57.879
Planes flew the precious fluid into Egypt.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:01.409
They brought thousands of needles, syringes,
other indispensible instruments.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:06.120
In record time, the Egyptian government had
the entire population immunized,

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:12.280
the sick put into isolation wards, and the
infected areas methodically disinfected.

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:14.280
The epidemic was checked,

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:18.200
and within three months completely eradicated
from Egypt.

00:20:35.139 --> 00:20:38.250
In the eternal battle a struggle has been
won,

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.520
won by international cooperation.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:47.140
But there is yet a tremendous task before
us, a task for all peoples, by all peoples.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:50.159
The lives of these little children too must
be saved,

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:54.280
that a light of hope may revive the courage
of those who suffer.

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:58.400
That mothers might yet smile in a new world.

